// Sounds, word shapes, sound changes and core vocabulary for generated
// languages.
//
// Every language draws its sounds from the phonemes below. Each phoneme has
// articulatory features; sound-change rules shift features ("voiced stops
// become fricatives between vowels"), so a change can only produce a sound
// that is listed here. `frequency` is the share of the world's languages that
// have the sound (roughly, after PHOIBLE), used when a new language family
// picks its inventory.
//
//   consonants: place  labial | dental | alveolar | palatal | velar | uvular | glottal
//               manner stop | affricate | fricative | nasal | lateral | rhotic | glide
//   vowels:     height high | mid | low;  backness front | central | back
//
// `text` is how the sound is written in the viewer (a simple romanization).
{
  "version": 1,
  "phonemes": [
    {"text": "p",  "kind": "consonant", "place": "labial",  "manner": "stop",      "voiced": false, "frequency": 0.86},
    {"text": "b",  "kind": "consonant", "place": "labial",  "manner": "stop",      "voiced": true,  "frequency": 0.63},
